I read the diff against `master` (8b0e1a1). I didn't run it. The fix looks right to me. It tracks the factory instance instead of a boolean flag, so if `view` is ever rebound, the new factory still gets its composer, and the existing behaviour stays the same.

One small thing in the new test: `countWildcardComposers()` calls `$property->setAccessible(true)` unconditionally. `ReflectionProperty::setAccessible()` has done nothing since PHP 8.1 and is deprecated in 8.5, and the CI matrix runs 8.5 and 8.6. The rest of the suite guards it, including `getInnerEngine()` in this same file:

```php
if (\PHP_VERSION_ID < 80100) {
    $property->setAccessible(true);
}
```

Using the same guard here would keep the new test from raising a deprecation on the 8.5/8.6 jobs once the workflows are approved.
